# citation.cff for the unconfoundedr package
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "unconfoundedr: Test Unconfoundedness by Comparing RCT and Observational Effects"
abstract: >
  R package to test (un)confoundedness by comparing a marginal treatment effect
  estimated in an RCT-like dataset with the same estimand from an observational
  dataset. Provides IPW and AIPW (doubly robust) estimators, percentile bootstrap
  confidence intervals for the effect difference, a Wald test, and optional
  transportability weighting (manual or auto-detected via KS/energy tests) with
  diagnostics for overlap and effective sample size.
authors:
  - family-names: Ribeiro
    given-names: Diogo
    email: dfr@esmad.ipp.pt          
    affiliation: ESMAD - IPP
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2025-08-29"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/diogoribeiro7/unconfoundedr"
url: "https://diogoribeiro7.github.io/unconfoundedr"
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - unconfoundedness
  - inverse probability weighting
  - augmented IPW
  - doubly robust
  - transportability
  - density ratio
  - bootstrap
  - R

preferred-citation:
